script = ExtResource("1_o5mip")
dialogue_id = "debate_ecological_instability"
record_title = "Debate Speech: The Ecological Report"
text = "PAGE: historian(PORTAL_NETWORK), AUDIENCE
historian: The most recent addition to our museum here is a letter written to a ruler from before the Shattering.
historian: It warns of rising seas and endless droughts.
historian: We have spent centuries telling ourselves that the Old World was a paradise, brought low by a sudden, mysterious disaster.
historian: But this letter tells a more mundane story.
historian: Our ancestors stripped the earth bare, and ignored the warnings until the ground beneath them gave way.
historian: The Scribe urges us to look backward, to emulate the majesty of those ancient empires and rebuild their unified world.
historian: But why would we want to rebuild a house built on a rotten foundation?
historian: We must stop viewing the world through the lens of ancient myths.
historian: We need to look at our soil, study our water, and understand the limits of our environment.
historian: If we blindly repeat the methods of the past, we will eventually run out of world to shatter."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://jtkfcsyiryo4"
